- Reuse/no-op results do not receive mutation attestations because no create/update was executed.

The two attestations must remain separate because:

- The action is an API endpoint choice and is not present in XML.
- A create result ID is server-assigned and cannot be in submitted XML.
- Update preservation deliberately echoes the current component/folder attributes rather than the requested placement.
- Live readback can contain server-assigned or normalized attributes, so comparing submitted bytes to readback bytes would report healthy applies as drift.

Verification must compare only live-at-apply and live-at-verify readback digests through `compare_live_build_provenance`. `digest=None` means unknown/unverifiable, never match. A non-`None` mismatch continues to raise `AUTHORING_LIVE_DEPLOYMENT_DRIFT`.

Placement resolution:

- Resolve `folder_name` at apply time to an exact, non-deleted, unique account folder.
- Do not use a silent “first name match” policy like the current helper behavior at `src/boomi_mcp/categories/components/folders.py:137-156`.
- Zero matches raise `PROCESS_MATERIALIZATION_PLACEMENT_NOT_FOUND`; multiple matches raise `PROCESS_MATERIALIZATION_PLACEMENT_AMBIGUOUS`.
- Create records the requested name and resolved ID.
- Update records the effective current placement preserved into the submitted XML, because requested placement is not merged by the current update policy.

